Robinhood Chain Insider Daily Recap

■ AI Agents & Infrastructure

@fobodotfun opened agent-only coin launches and trading on https://t.co/rqnWdw5hkf, requiring ERC-8004 identities for AI agents, in collaboration with @OakAgentKit and @HoodLockRH.

@OakAgentKit confirmed the integration, with agents carrying verifiable onchain identities and every action requiring user approval.

@corbelfinance launched Corbel x402, enabling AI agents to pay for tool calls in USDG without accounts or API keys, covering token checks, risk analysis, charts, and order planning.

@getleash_app went live on Robinhood Chain with an AI agent security firewall featuring Safe wallets, user-defined limits, and protection against unauthorized or risky transactions.

@Polydash_ introduced agent launches on Polypad, combining ERC-8004 identities, reputation scores, capped session keys, and locked tokenized funds with a two-day public waiting period.

■ DeFi & Tokenized Assets

@arcus_xyz integrated @RobinhoodCrypto Stock Tokens as collateral for stablecoin borrowing through Morpho-powered credit markets.

@SurplusRH enabled AI agents to execute swaps on Robinhood Chain through @rialto_xyz routing.

@kairo_market announced its migration from Arc to Robinhood Chain at a 1:1 conversion ratio, alongside a separate UON airdrop for eligible holders based on a December 15 snapshot.

@reppo set December 2 for its planned EVAL migration to Robinhood Chain, with a fixed 8,500 token supply, staking rewards in daily API credits, and a 2x credit boost during the first month.

■ Launches & Ecosystem Expansion

@rarible brought its Digital Humans collection of 5,000 Shadow universe characters to Robinhood Chain.

@AltDeckListing added Good In The Hood ($GOOD) to its listing platform.

■ Community & Token Economics

@ZokiEth kicked off a Thanksgiving contest offering up to $100 in robinhood:0x54a557dc542676f56ce2b1b5807cc76bedca308a prizes for submissions showcasing real-world token utility.

@fobodotfun detailed its anti-snipe mechanism for new launches: a 90% starting tax that declines to 2.5% over 60 seconds, with 60% directed toward the token’s floor and 40% allocated to robinhood:0x000de658153f47f23e92973c8eb1e89762703676 buybacks and burns.

